            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you put an expandable hose on a reel?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No. Expandable hoses contract into an irregular bunched shape that will not wind evenly on a drum, and the winding tension damages the latex tube inside. Store expandable hoses in a hose pot, a bucket, or on a wide-radius hook instead, and drain them fully before storage.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Why does my hose reel leak?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Almost always the swivel joint where water passes from the fixed inlet into the rotating drum, which contains seals that wear over time. On a quality reel with a brass swivel, replacement seals are inexpensive and easy to fit. On a reel with a sealed plastic swivel assembly, the leak usually means replacing the reel.
              </p>
